-- A type error in a mixfix call is reported over the whole call, from its
-- first argument to its last.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
a `plus` b MEANS a + b

-- four inputs for a rule of two
tooMany MEANS 1 `plus` 2 `plus` 3

-- a number where a condition is needed
notACondition MEANS IF 1 `plus` 2 THEN 1 ELSE 2

-- four inputs for a rule of two, one of them a string
wrongKind MEANS 1 `plus` "x" `plus` 3
